From 5c2f36682acb8408bf9630e2390a02e1e9320588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam James <sam@gentoo.org>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 13:51:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] gtype: downgrade some (non-*_get_type) G_GNUC_CONST ->
 G_GNUC_PURE

g_type_check_is_value_type and g_type_test_flags both read global memory,
so can't be const. They only seem to write for the purpose of a lock, which
they undo at the end, so maybe we can get away with G_GNUC_PURE here.

