From: Philip Withnall <pwithnall@gnome.org>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 18:04:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] codegen: Drop an inappropriate G_GNUC_CONST from inside a
 code comment

Might as well have this comment reflect reality (see the previous few
commits).

Signed-off-by: Philip Withnall <pwithnall@gnome.org>
---
 gio/gdbus-2.0/codegen/dbustypes.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gio/gdbus-2.0/codegen/dbustypes.py b/gio/gdbus-2.0/codegen/dbustypes.py
index 21f0901fe5..ae6c048c6c 100644
--- a/gio/gdbus-2.0/codegen/dbustypes.py
+++ b/gio/gdbus-2.0/codegen/dbustypes.py
@@ -595,7 +595,7 @@ class Property:
             self.name_lower = utils.camel_case_to_uscore(name).lower().replace("-", "_")
         self.name_hyphen = self.name_lower.replace("_", "-")
         # don't clash with the GType getter, e.g.:
-        # GType foo_bar_get_type (void); G_GNUC_CONST
+        # GType foo_bar_get_type (void);
         if self.name_lower == "type":
             self.name_lower = "type_"
 
